  "beats": [
   {
    "id": "b01",
    "slot": "hook.question_reveal",
    "start": 0.6,
    "end": 10.6,
    "audio_s": 10.0,
    "words": 27,
    "wpm": 162,
    "pause_after": 0.6,
    "think": 0.0,
    "text": "Does twice the voltage always mean twice the current? Here is a resistor of ten ohms with two volts across it. Now we make it four volts."
   },
   {
    "id": "b02",
    "slot": "check.predict",
    "start": 11.2,
    "end": 17.12,
    "audio_s": 5.92,
    "words": 14,
    "wpm": 142,
    "pause_after": 0.3,
    "think": 5.0,
    "text": "Pause and predict the current at four volts. Then decide whether always is safe."
   },
   {
    "id": "b03",
    "slot": "explain.ladder_step",
    "start": 22.42,
    "end": 32.42,
    "audio_s": 10.0,
    "words": 25,
    "wpm": 150,
    "pause_after": 0.5,
    "think": 0.0,
    "text": "At two volts, the current is zero point two amperes. At four volts, it is zero point four amperes. Twice the voltage, twice the current."
   },
   {
    "id": "b04",
    "slot": "explain.ladder_step",
    "start": 32.92,
    "end": 45.56,
    "audio_s": 12.64,
    "words": 27,
    "wpm": 128,
    "pause_after": 0.8,
    "think": 0.0,
    "text": "For this resistor at constant temperature, voltage divided by current stays ten ohms at both points. That constant is the resistance: voltage equals current multiplied by resistance."
   },
   {
    "id": "b05",
    "slot": "misconception.confront",
    "start": 46.36,
    "end": 56.6,
    "audio_s": 10.24,
    "words": 25,
    "wpm": 146,
    "pause_after": 0.8,
    "think": 0.0,
    "text": "But always is not safe. A filament bulb gets hot, so its resistance rises, and the current no longer doubles. The rule needs constant resistance."
   },
   {
    "id": "b06",
    "slot": "recap.statement",
    "start": 57.4,
    "end": 65.32,
    "audio_s": 7.92,
    "words": 18,
    "wpm": 136,
    "pause_after": 0.6,
    "think": 0.0,
    "text": "So, for a conductor at constant temperature, current is proportional to voltage, and resistance is the constant ratio."
   },
   {
    "id": "b07",
    "slot": "outro.disclosure",
    "start": 65.92,
    "end": 69.92,
    "audio_s": 4.0,
    "words": 5,
